{
  "raw": {
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/cbu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/1459": {
      "title": "Sessional Instructors in Mi'kmaq Studies",
      "description": "Sessional Instructors in Mi'kmaq Studies | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs CBU home English (United States) Sign In Sessional Instructors in Mi'kmaq Studies Req #222 Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada Apply Share Job Description Posted Tuesday, September 1, 2026 at 7:00 PM | Expires Friday, November 6, 2026 at 6:59 PM EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY All required documents must be uploaded to Additional Documents with correct titles for each required document. Cape Breton University’s Mi’kmaq Studies and Unama’ki College are seeking applicants interested in teaching specific courses in the fall or winter term on campus, online, or in community. We are seeking qualified L’nu sessional instructors who may be available to teach courses that become available over the next two years. We anticipate ongoing teaching needs in areas such as: Mi’kmaw Language classes Mi’kmaw History classes Mi’kmaw Traditional Governance Other areas of Mi’kmaw knowledge and expertise This is an excellent opportunity for individuals who are interested in exploring a future teaching career, while sharing their knowledge and experience with students. If you are thinking of possible future at CBU, this is a great way to see if teaching is for you! The ideal candidates will possess: A graduate degree in a relevant discipline; and/or applicants who do not hold a Master's degree but have significant traditional, cultural, community-based, or professional knowledge will also be considered for courses that align with their area of expertise. Experience teaching in First Nations communities; Relevant qualifications, experience, or demonstrated expertise in the subject area being taught . TEACHING ON CAMPUS: MI’KMAQ STUDIES Situated within the School of Arts and Social Science (SASS), Mi’kmaq Studies advances Mi’kmaw knowledge and scholarship in support of students developing academic critical thinking skills and awareness of Mi’kmaw perspectives and knowledges. Mi’kmaq Studies fosters engaged citizens who can interact respectfully with Mi’kmaw communities, contribute to self-determination, and understand the importance of upholding treaty and rights-based responsibilities. It is available as a major, double major, and concentration in the Bachelor of Arts (BA) and as a major or double major in the Bachelor of Arts Community Studies (BACS). We are seeking instructors who can teach in this area on campus, and sometimes online. Fall and winter courses typically run for 12 weeks. TEACHING OFF-CAMPUS: IN-COMMUNITY PROGRAMMING For more than 30 years, Unama’ki College’s In-Community Degree Programs have been making post-secondary education more accessible to Indigenous students by offering tailored degree programming across Mi’kma’ki. Students have the opportunity to earn a degree from CBU while studying at home, close to their families and supports systems in addition to receiving specialized student support from CBU. We seek instructors who are interested in teaching courses in-community, which are taught in a more condensed timeline (4 to 8 weeks). Applications for the successful candidate will include a: cover letter describing the expertise of the applicant complete resume list of at least three references. Please upload all required documents to Additional Documents if no designated area is listed . Incomplete applications may not be considered. Applications will be accepted on an ongoing basis and will be reviewed as teaching opportunities arise. To learn more about these opportunities, prospective applicants are invited to attend one of two online information sessions. Details, including dates and times, will be posted on the Unama’ki College Facebook page . Cape Breton University is strongly committed to fostering diversity within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, visible minorities, Indigenous peoples, persons with disabilities, and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply but applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. CBU is committed to Equity, Diversity, and Inclusion (EDI) and applicants are encouraged to self-identity if they are part of a marginalised community, or have experience working with Indigenous communities. If we contact you for an interview and you are a person with a disability who requires technical aids or alternative arrangements, please let us know of these needs and how we can be of assistance. Cape Breton University Human Resources Dept. HumanResources@cbu.ca 1250 Grand Lake Road, Sydney, NS B1M 1A2 Job Details Job Family Sessionals Pay Type Salary Scan this QR code and apply! Download Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Statement of Accessibility Cookie Preferences Delete Application Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow us to share information with third party advertising and analytics partners and use your information for advertising and analytics purposes. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/cbu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/1512": {
      "title": "Campus Security Officer",
      "description": "Campus Security Officer | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs CBU home English (United States) Sign In Campus Security Officer Req #230 Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada Apply Share Job Description Posted Wednesday, October 7, 2026 at 7:00 PM | Expires Friday, October 23, 2026 at 6:59 PM EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY Please ensure you upload your resume, attach a cover letter,  list of references in the correct upload area. Any other documents required please add to Additional Documents. CAMPUS SECURITY OFFICER Cape Breton University (CBU) invites applications for the position of Campus Security Officer within the Emergency Management & Security Services department. This is a full-time continuing position . Cape Breton University (CBU) is committed to providing a safe and secure environment for employees and students to work, study, and live. CBU has established a proactive Campus Safety program aimed at education and fostering a safe environment for all. PURPOSE: Under the general supervision of the Emergency Management & Security Services Manager, the Campus Security Officer is responsible for fostering a safe, secure, and inclusive campus community through education, prevention, and the enforcement of university regulations. This position is critical to maintaining continuous 24/7 campus security coverage, ensuring operational continuity and the university’s ability to respond effectively to emergencies without interruption. The Campus Security Officer exercises independent judgment and sound decision- making in alignment with established policies and procedures, ensuring appropriate escalation and communication, particularly during emergent and high-risk situations, and may be required to provide immediate response activities and coordination until emergency services arrive. The role supports the university, and is accountable for timely response, accurate reporting, and adherence to established procedures. This is a physically demanding role requiring work in a fast-paced, high-pressure environment, including the ability to work the required rotating shifts (days, nights, weekends, and holidays). SPECIFIC RESPONSIBILITIES: Security Services Promote the safety and security of students, staff, visitors, and University property. Respond to, assess, and coordinate incidents and emergencies, including initial scene control, fact gathering, documentation, and reporting. Assist with other investigative activities as assigned Exercise independent judgment while escalating incidents in accordance with established protocols and maintaining communication with supervisors. Monitor and control access points; lock and unlock facilities based on operational schedules. Conduct proactive patrols, monitor facilities and access points, and ensure the physical security of campus property. Build positive relationships and provide assistance, information, and support to staff, students, and visitors. Serve as a operational contact for Casual Campus Security Officers, providing guidance, mentorship, and support. Collaborate with internal departments to support coordinated responses to safety, behavioral, and wellness concerns. Prepare clear, accurate, and thorough reports, and preserve evidence as required. Maintain confidentiality and handle sensitive information in accordance with privacy legislation and university policies. Operate within the scope of authority defined by CBU Policies, other applicable legislation and Special Constable appointment, using appropriate and proportionate response measures. Administer First Aid/CPR and coordinate responses with emergency services (police, fire, EHS). Monitor and assist individuals in distress, ensuring appropriate intervention and escalation. Conduct traffic/parking enforcement. Conduct crowd and event coordination activities. Participate in fire safety programs, alarm testing, and emergency preparedness activities. On occasion, assist with conducting security audits and inspections, identifying risks and recommending corrective action Inspect safety equipment (e.g., fire extinguishers, AEDs) for operational readiness. Participate in the Safe Walk/Work Safe Program. Support operational continuity through consistent application of procedures and knowledge of campus-specific risks. Perform other related safety, security, and emergency coordination duties as assigned to support operational requirements. Education and Engagement Support and deliver safety education programs for students and staff, including: Personal safety and campus security Alcohol and drug awareness Sexual violence prevention and response Residence safety Emergency preparedness Promote awareness, engagement, and community trust through proactive outreach. QUALIFICATIONS AND SKILLS: Diploma or Certificate in policing, corrections, criminology, or equivalent experience. Minimum of 2 years’ experience in policing, corrections, or security services. Valid CPR, First Aid, and AED certification (or ability to obtain). Valid driver’s license with a clean abstract. Ability to obtain and maintain: Criminal Record Check Special Constable status (Applicable to Full-Time position only Core Competencies Demonstrated initiative and proactive approach to safety and security. Strong attention to detail, particularly in documentation and reporting. Effective interpersonal and communication skills, with strong de-escalation abilities. Comfortable using security-related technology to support daily operations, including CCTV and camera systems, access control systems, Microsoft 365, and electronic reporting and records management platforms. Physically capable of performing operational duties, including prolonged periods of activity and responding effectively to emergency situations. Proven ability to work in fast-paced, high-pressure environments and make sound decisions under stress. Experienced in shift work, including days, nights, weekends, and holidays in a fast-paced environment. Strong situational awareness and risk assessment skills. Professionalism, integrity, and confidentiality. Resilience and composure in stressful or potentially traumatic situations. Maintain all required certifications and competencies. Participate in ongoing training and professional development to support operational effectiveness. Willingness to complete additional training as required. Applications for the successful candidate will include a: cover letter describing the expertise of the applicant complete resume list of at least three references. Short listed candidates will be required to submit three reference letters. Please upload all required documents to Additional Documents if no designated area is listed . Incomplete applications will not be considered. Applications must be received by October 23, 2026 Select Apply above to start your application today! The union affiliation for this position is with the Nova Scotia Government & General Employees Union, Local 18, MOS. Cape Breton University is strongly committed to fostering diversity within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, visible minorities, Indigenous peoples, persons with disabilities, and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply but applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. CBU is committed to Equity, Diversity, and Inclusion (EDI) and applicants are encouraged to self-identity if they are part of a marginalised community, or have experience working with Indigenous communities. If we contact you for an interview and you are a person with a disability who requires technical aids or alternative arrangements, please let us know of these needs and how we can be of assistance. Cape Breton University Human Resources Dept. HumanResouces@cbu.ca 1250 Grand Lake Road, Sydney, NS B1M 1A2 Scan this QR code and apply! Download Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Statement of Accessibility Cookie Preferences Delete Application Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/cbu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/1501": {
      "title": "Field Education Lead, BSW",
      "description": "Field Education Lead, BSW | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs CBU home English (United States) Sign In Field Education Lead, BSW Req #231 Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada Apply Share Job Description Posted Monday, October 5, 2026 at 7:00 PM | Expires Wednesday, October 28, 2026 at 6:59 PM EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY Please ensure you upload your resume, attach a cover letter,  list of references in the correct upload area. Any other documents required please add to Additional Documents. Cape Breton University (CBU) invites applications for a Full-Time Continuing, Field Education Lead in the Department of Social Work, School of Arts and Social Sciences . The successful candidate will provide leadership for the management, administration, educational quality, and community relationships that support field education within the BSW program. They will ensure that student practicums, field-related courses, policies, documentation, and evaluation processes align with CASWE accreditation standards, the CASWE Core Learning Objectives, institutional policies, and the mission and goals of the BSW program. Position Responsibilities: Reporting to and working with the Program Director, the Field Education Lead creates, facilitates, and assesses field practicum placements for social work students. Responsibilities include: Lead the management, administration, educational development, and evaluation of BSW field education, ensuring alignment with CASWE standards, Core Learning Objectives, institutional policies, and program outcomes. Maintain and oversee field education policies, procedures, documentation, learning contracts, evaluation processes, and related materials . Recruit, assess, approve, develop, support, and retain practicum agencies and qualified field supervisors , and assess placement capacity for Field Practicum I and II. Coordinate student placement processes , including meeting with students, assessing placement fit, managing placement decisions, and communicating with students, agencies, supervisors, and the Field Practice Educator. Support placement managers and field supervisors regarding practicum expectations, supervision, student learning, policies, documentation, and evaluation responsibilities . Ensure required student screening and placement documentation is completed and collaborate with the Field Practice Educator to address concerns related to student performance, conduct, attendance, supervision, safety, learning opportunities, or placement suitability. Build and maintain community partnerships with social workers and practicum settings and identify opportunities and trends to strengthen field education. Support professional development, research, collaborative initiatives, and university service related to the BSW program and community partnerships. Qualifications of this role are: Master of Social Work Degree (MSW); A minimum of five years of practice experience in the field of social work ; Understanding of social services, practice and placement requirements and standards , and current issues and trends in social work; Demonstrated commitment to the principles of social work education and practice , including, but not limited to, social justice, equity, diversity, inclusion, and decolonization; Understanding of social work education and practice in the context of rural, indigenous, and marginal communities at the micro, mezzo, and macro levels; Ability to work independently and as a team member , including the ability to develop interpersonal, collegial, and relationship-building skills suited to field education, social work education, university, and professional contexts; Flexibility with hours of work based on program operation needs (e.g., special events in the evening, early morning preparation for daytime special events, etc.); Ability to multitask priorities and responsibilities. Applications for the successful candidate will include: a cover letter describing the expertise of the applicant a complete resume (or CV) A list of least three references. All required documents must be uploaded to \"Additional Documents\" with correct titles for each required document. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, priority will be given to Canadian citizens and permanent residents. Applications must be received by 11:00PM on October 28th, 2026. Cape Breton University is strongly committed to fostering diversity within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, visible minorities, Indigenous peoples, persons with disabilities, and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply but applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. CBU is committed to Equity, Diversity, and Inclusion (EDI) and applicants are encouraged to self-identity if they are part of a marginalised community, or have experience working with Indigenous communities. If we contact you for an interview and you are a person with a disability who requires technical aids or alternative arrangements, please let us know of these needs and how we can be of assistance. Cape Breton University Human Resources Dept. HumanResouces@cbu.ca 1250 Grand Lake Road, Sydney, NS B1M 1A2 Scan this QR code and apply! Download Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Statement of Accessibility Cookie Preferences Delete Application Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/cbu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/1545": {
      "title": "Lab Instructor, Biology (Limited Term)",
      "description": "Lab Instructor, Biology (Limited Term) | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs CBU home English (United States) Sign In Lab Instructor, Biology (Limited Term) Req #226 Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada Apply Share Job Description Posted Thursday, October 15, 2026 at 7:00 PM | Expires Wednesday, January 6, 2027 at 6:59 PM EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY Please ensure you upload your resume, attach a cover letter,  list of references in the correct upload area. Any other documents required please add to Additional Documents. The Department of Biology in the School of Science & Technology at CBU invites applications for a Full-Time Limited Term position in Biology at the rank of Lab Instructor for approximately 8 Months . This position will commence August 1, 2027 (or as soon as possible thereafter). One of Canada’s youngest and most ambitious universities, CBU recognizes its location on Cape Breton Island as part of Mi’kma’ki, the ancestral and unceded territory of the Mi’kmaq people. CBU offers a comprehensive set of liberal arts, science, and professional programs and a unique commitment to community, economic development, aboriginal learning, and research into many aspects of environment and culture. CBU delivers an authentic multicultural experience to all who become part of its academic community. Surrounded by pristine natural landscape, vibrant culture, and welcoming communities on Canada’s stunning east coast, CBU attracts students from more than 50 countries around the world . Our faculty bring passion to their teaching and research, and we are known for our friendly and inclusive culture. Strong community involvement and a spirit of entrepreneurship enhance CBU's position in post-secondary education. The successful candidate will perform the duties outlined in Article 25.1.2 in the CBU Faculty Association Collective Agreement. Topics of focus shall include, but may not be limited to, Physiology, Invertebrate Zoology, Marine Ecology, and Plant Ecology. Candidates shall, as a minimum requirement, possess a B.Sc. in Biology. An M.Sc. in Biology is preferred. Previous lab instructor experience at the post-secondary level considered an asset but not mandatory. CBU teaches programs on campus, off campus in locations across and outside of Canada, and on-line. The university and its partners will therefore provide opportunities for faculty members to teach in different modes in different locations as part of their regular workload. While these opportunities may not be available equally for all faculty positions in all programs, a clear willingness to teach in different modes and locations will be noted as part of your application. Applications for the successful candidate will include: a letter of application quoting the reference number a copy of academic transcripts a complete dossier including curriculum vitae (or resume) evidence of effective teaching a statement of teaching philosophy a diversity statement A list of least three references. Short listed candidates will be required to submit three reference letters. Applicants are expected to demonstrate potential and commitment with regard to teaching activities and service to Cape Breton University, community and profession. Please upload all required documents to Additional Documents if no designated area is listed . Incomplete applications may not be considered. How to Apply select Apply on the top of page to begin your application. Applications must be received by Jan 6, 2027 at 11:59:59PM . The union affiliation of this position is with the Cape Breton University Faculty Association. Cape Breton University is strongly committed to fostering diversity within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, visible minorities, Indigenous peoples, persons with disabilities, and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply but applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. CBU is committed to Equity, Diversity, and Inclusion (EDI) and applicants are encouraged to self-identity if they are part of a marginalised community, or have experience working with Indigenous communities. If we contact you for an interview and you are a person with a disability who requires technical aids or alternative arrangements, please let us know of these needs and how we can be of assistance. Cape Breton University Human Resources Dept. HumanResouces@cbu.ca 1250 Grand Lake Road, Sydney, NS B1M 1A2 Scan this QR code and apply! Download Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Statement of Accessibility Cookie Preferences Delete Application Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/cbu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/1540": {
      "title": "Recruitment & Engagement Specialist",
      "description": "Recruitment & Engagement Specialist - Western Canada | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs CBU home English (United States) Sign In Recruitment & Engagement Specialist - Western Canada Req #235 Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada Apply Share Job Description Posted Wednesday, October 14, 2026 at 7:00 PM | Expires Monday, October 26, 2026 at 6:59 PM EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY Please ensure you upload your resume, attach a cover letter,  list of references in the correct upload area. Any other documents required please add to Additional Documents. JOB DESCRIPTION PURPOSE: To develop and coordinate recruitment activities and strengthen strategic partnerships for Cape Breton University primarily in Western Canada. This position strengthens CBU’s student recruitment and community engagement efforts in Western Canada by increasing CBU’s presence in the market, nurturing relationships with partner institutions and establishing and leveraging transfer pathways. The Recruitment and Engagement Specialist position directly contributes to the university’s objective to attract more domestic students by enabling greater reach, increasing supports for prospective students and by growing CBU’s strategic partnerships. SPECIFIC RESPONSIBILITIES: Develop and manage operational recruitment and engagement strategies for Western Canada that support the university’s overall strategic enrollment management plan. Work with Marketing Manager to execute marketing strategy for the Western Canada region along with advising on the use of marketing channels to reach target audiences (social media, digital advertising, out-of-home, etc.) Work with internal stakeholders, including Deans and faculty members, to develop program-specific recruitment and engagement plans that are relevant to the industry and to the local market. Building and nurturing relationships with key stakeholders for direct-entry prospective students (Guidance Counsellors, Teachers, Administrators, Coaches) Building and nurturing relationships with key stakeholders for transfer prospective students (College Pathways Managers, Academic Partnership Coordinators, and Centres for Education) Engaging prospective students and their influencers with 1:1 meetings, information sessions, engagement events, and on-campus tours when applicable Work closely with internal stakeholders to develop a strategic plan to attract and support both students of African descent and Indigenous students from Western Canada. Travel within Western Canada to deliver recruitment presentations, attend education fairs, and participate in other engagement activities. Manage logistics of CBU owned events and brand activations at partner or industry events. Work with alumni office to develop relationships with CBU alumni to assist with recruitment activities and alumni engagement. Liaise regularly with fellow Recruitment & Engagement team members across Canada and with the Manager, Domestic Recruitment to ensure regional priorities and activations ladder up to national objectives and strategic enrollment goals. Collaborate with other CBU departments to review and improve prospective student experience from the point of inquiry through the student lifecycle. Undertake market research to drive student recruitment, brand development, regional sponsorships and strategic partnership development. Analyze this recruitment data and enrollment trends using CRM (Recruit) and Microsoft Excel, to inform the development and execution of recruitment and marketing plans related to strategic enrollment management goals. Manage budgets related to recruitment and engagement efforts in the Western Canada market. Play an active role in representing CBU at events and stakeholder engagement opportunities. Must uphold the University’s obligations to confidentiality and protection of personal information. Other related duties as required. QUALIFICATIONS & SKILLS: Completion of an undergraduate degree with preference given to additional relevant postgraduate education or qualifications Minimum of 5 years’ of related experience. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills (oral and written). Excellent time management skills. Experience developing and managing relationships with partners and key stakeholders. Experience working within an integrated marketing and communications team. Experience working in a goal-oriented sales and business development environment. Experience managing small to medium sized stakeholder engagement events. Ability to identify, prioritize, and manage multiple strategic initiatives that support the university’s strategic enrollment management plan. Ability to work independently and manage workload, identifying and prioritizing CBU’s needs within the market, while contributing to a positive and collaborative team environment. Ability to build and nurture dynamic partnerships and relationships with internal and external stakeholders. Ability to relate and respond to diverse student populations. Ability to analyze and leverage data to inform strategy that aligns to national domestic recruitment goals, informed by CBU’s strategic enrollment management plan. Ability to critically review and advise on sponsorship and partnership opportunities, leading activation and relationship management strategies. Ability to develop and communicate relevant insights based on research and experience to inform strategic planning and development of marketing and recruitment plans. Proficient with Microsoft Office programs, web platforms, and experience working in a Customer Service Management software. Ability to accommodate flexible work hours, including evenings and weekends, as necessary. Current driver’s license with the ability and willingness to travel. Applications must be received by October 26 th 2026 . Press Apply at the op of the page to submit your application today. Cape Breton University is strongly committed to fostering diversity within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, visible minorities, Indigenous peoples, persons with disabilities, and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply but applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. CBU is committed to Equity, Diversity, and Inclusion (EDI) and applicants are encouraged to self-identity if they are part of a marginalised community, or have experience working with Indigenous communities. If we contact you for an interview and you are a person with a disability who requires technical aids or alternative arrangements, please let us know of these needs and how we can be of assistance. Cape Breton University Human Resources Dept. HumanResouces@cbu.ca 1250 Grand Lake Road, Sydney, NS B1M 1A2 Scan this QR code and apply! Download Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Statement of Accessibility Cookie Preferences Delete Application Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/cbu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/1536": {
      "title": "Recruitment & Engagement Specialist-African NS & Canadian Students",
      "description": "Recruitment & Engagement Specialist-African NS & Canadian Students | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs CBU home English (United States) Sign In Recruitment & Engagement Specialist-African NS & Canadian Students Req #236 Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada Apply Share Job Description Posted Wednesday, October 14, 2026 at 7:00 PM | Expires Monday, October 26, 2026 at 6:59 PM EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY Please ensure you upload your resume, attach a cover letter,  list of references in the correct upload area. Any other documents required please add to Additional Documents. JOB DESCRIPTION PURPOSE: To develop and coordinate recruitment activities and strengthen strategic partnerships for Cape Breton University to help increase African Nova Scotian & Canadian student enrolment specifically in the Bachelor of Science, Nursing program. SPECIFIC RESPONSIBILITIES: Develop and manage the execution of an African Nova Scotian & Canadian enrolment plan. Develop and execute the operational recruitment plan for the direct from high school, mature and articulation partners markets. Work with Marketing Manager to develop a marketing strategy for African Nova Scotian and Canadian students. Oversee budget related to African Nova Scotian & Canadian Recruitment activity. Provide quality customer service to prospective students, their influencers, and the public. Explore, confirm, and co-ordinate relationship building activities with guidance counsellors, teachers, and administrators within Nova Scotia. Nurture relationships with prospective African Nova Scotian and Canadian students from the first point of contact through to enrolment ensuring a positive brand experience. Develop and maintain a positive relationship with the African Nova Scotian Organizations, and Centre for Education and Government Departments. Work closely with internal stakeholders, specifically the Student Development Officer for Students of African Descent and the Program Coordinator – African Nova Scotian Youth, to develop a strategic plan to attract and support students of African descent. Travel within the province of Nova Scotia to deliver recruitment presentations, attend education fairs and participate in other engagement activities. Work with alumni office to develop relationships with CBU alumni to assist with recruitment activities and alumni engagement. Undertake market research related to student recruitment. Analyze, understand, and apply current and historical enrolment data in combination with demographics to determine trends, forecast future opportunities and inform strategy development. Maintain a timely and accurate communication and reporting structure with the Manager of Canadian Recruitment. Work within the Customer Relationship Management System Recruit to nurture student leads. Utilize social media platforms (Facebook, Twitter, Instagram) to assist in the recruitment of African Nova Scotian & Canadian students and the promotion of CBU, while contributing to departmental social media groups, responding to inquiries as quickly as possible and supporting the execution of digital recruitment initiatives as assigned. Must uphold the University’s obligations to confidentiality and protection of personal information. Other related duties as required. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS Completion of an undergraduate degree or combination of education with experience (CBU graduate preferred). A minimum of five years working experience in a dynamic environment especially managing stakeholder relations, leading, and executing events and providing quality customer service and support. Experience in post-secondary education considered an asset. Must be historically connected to one of the 52 African communities in Nova Scotia. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills (oral and written). Excellent time management skills. Ability to work independently and in a team environment. Ability to relate and respond to diverse student populations. Ability to accommodate flexible work hours, including evenings and weekends, as necessary. Experience working in a Customer Service Management software considered an asset. Applications must be received by October 26th 2026. Press Apply on the top of page to submit your application. Cape Breton University is strongly committed to fostering diversity within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, visible minorities, Indigenous peoples, persons with disabilities, and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply but applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. CBU is committed to Equity, Diversity, and Inclusion (EDI) and applicants are encouraged to self-identity if they are part of a marginalised community, or have experience working with Indigenous communities. If we contact you for an interview and you are a person with a disability who requires technical aids or alternative arrangements, please let us know of these needs and how we can be of assistance. Cape Breton University Human Resources Dept. HumanResouces@cbu.ca 1250 Grand Lake Road, Sydney, NS B1M 1A2 Scan this QR code and apply! Download Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Statement of Accessibility Cookie Preferences Delete Application Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/cbu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/1527": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Nursing (Limited Term)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Nursing (Limited Term) | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs CBU home English (United States) Sign In Assistant Professor, Nursing (Limited Term) Req #241 Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada Apply Share Job Description Posted Wednesday, October 14, 2026 at 7:00 PM | Expires Friday, November 13, 2026 at 6:59 PM EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY Please ensure you upload your resume, attach a cover letter,  list of references in the correct upload area. Any other documents required please add to Additional Documents. The School of Nursing at Cape Breton University (CBU) invite applications for 1 Limited Term position at the rank of Assistant Professor for approximately 1 year. This position will commence December 1, 2026 (or soon thereafter). One of Canada’s youngest and most ambitious universities, CBU recognizes its location on Cape Breton Island as part of Mi’kma’ki, the ancestral and unceded territory of the Mi’kmaq people. CBU offers a comprehensive set of liberal arts, science, and professional programs and a unique commitment to community, economic development, aboriginal learning, and research into many aspects of environment and culture. CBU delivers an authentic multicultural experience to all who become part of its academic community. Surrounded by pristine natural landscape, vibrant culture, and welcoming communities on Canada’s stunning east coast, CBU attracts students from more than 50 countries around the world. Our faculty bring passion to their teaching and research and we are known for our friendly and inclusive culture. Strong community involvement and a spirit of entrepreneurship enhance CBU's position in post-secondary education. Cape Breton University is committed to championing the Island’s prosperity by bolstering the overall health and development of Cape Breton Island. The School of Nursing is at the heart of this commitment, helping to meet the evolving needs of the healthcare system in Cape Breton and across the Province of Nova Scotia through innovative research and teaching. CBU’s connection with the Eastern Zone of Nova Scotia Health creates diverse practice-learning opportunities for students specifically in rural, urban and Indigenous health specialties. The School of Nursing is seeking one dynamic registered nurse to become a member of a progressive, energetic and research-focused department. Teaching in a concept-based curriculum, the nursing faculty seeks candidates whose philosophy and commitment are complementary. In addition to teaching and research, the successful candidates may be required to participate in nursing practice with groups of students in various practice settings, simulation and/or labs. Applicants are expected to demonstrate potential and commitment with regard to teaching, research/creative/scholarly activities and service to Cape Breton University, community and profession. Successful candidates will have: An undergraduate/graduate degree in nursing (i.e. BScN, MN); A completed PhD or other Doctoral degree in a health-related field or education; A minimum of five years’ experience as a Registered Nurse; An active practicing unrestricted RN license with the Nova Scotia College of Nursing (or be eligible for) prior to commencement of this position; Demonstrated excellence in classroom teaching and mentorship; A commitment to nursing scholarship and research; Experience in theory-based classroom teaching. Applications for the successful candidate will include an: cover letter describing the expertise of the applicant statement of teaching philosophy statement of research complete CV including a list of publications evidence of effective teaching list of least three references. Please upload all required documents to Additional Documents if no designated area is listed. Incomplete applications will not be considered. The union affiliation of this position is with the Cape Breton University Faculty Association. Applications must be received by 11:00PM on November 13 th 2026. Cape Breton University is strongly committed to fostering diversity within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, visible minorities, Indigenous peoples, persons with disabilities, and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply but applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. CBU is committed to Equity, Diversity, and Inclusion (EDI) and applicants are encouraged to self-identity if they are part of a marginalised community, or have experience working with Indigenous communities. If we contact you for an interview and you are a person with a disability who requires technical aids or alternative arrangements, please let us know of these needs and how we can be of assistance. Cape Breton University Human Resources Dept. HumanResouces@cbu.ca 1250 Grand Lake Road, Sydney, NS B1M 1A2 Scan this QR code and apply! Download Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Statement of Accessibility Cookie Preferences Delete Application Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/cbu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/1522": {
      "title": "Sessional Theory Instructor",
      "description": "Sessional Theory Instructor - School of Nursing | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs CBU home English (United States) Sign In Sessional Theory Instructor - School of Nursing Req #238 Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada Apply Share Job Description Posted Thursday, October 8, 2026 at 7:00 PM | Expires Thursday, December 31, 2026 at 6:59 PM EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY Please ensure you upload your resume, attach a cover letter,  list of references in the correct upload area. Any other documents required please add to Additional Documents. Sessional Theory Instructors Cape Breton University invites expressions of interest from qualified nurse educators interested in serving as Theory Instructors within the School of Nursing . These appointments are made on an as-needed basis to address teaching vacancies throughout the academic year. Position Overview The School of Nursing maintains a pool of qualified instructors who may be appointed to teach theory courses when vacancies arise. Successful candidates may be hired to teach a specific course within the Nursing program for a designated academic term, depending on program needs and faculty workload requirements. Course assignments may vary and could include theory courses offered throughout the undergraduate Nursing program. Responsibilities The Sessional Theory Instructor will: Deliver course content in accordance with approved course outlines and program objectives. Facilitate student learning through lectures, discussions, and other instructional methods. Develop and administer course evaluations, assignments, and examinations as required. Assess student performance and provide timely feedback. Maintain accurate academic records and submit final grades in accordance with university policies. Participate in course-related activities and communicate regularly with students and School of Nursing faculty. Foster an inclusive and supportive learning environment. Qualifications Applicants must possess: A Master's degree in Nursing or a related discipline . Proof of current RN registration/licensure Demonstrated knowledge and expertise in nursing theory and practice. Preference may be given to applicants with: Previous post-secondary teaching experience. Experience in curriculum delivery and student evaluation. Expertise in areas relevant to the identified course vacancy. Strong communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills. Applications for the successful candidate will include a: A cover letter outlining teaching interests and qualifications. A current curriculum vitae (CV). Copies of relevant academic credentials. Contact information for three professional references. Applications will be retained for consideration as teaching opportunities arise within the School of Nursing. Please upload all required documents to Additional Documents if no designated area is listed . Incomplete applications will not be considered. Applications will be reviewed as clinical instructional needs arise. Applicant pool is open until December 31, 2026. Cape Breton University is strongly committed to fostering diversity within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, visible minorities, Indigenous peoples, persons with disabilities, and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply but applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. CBU is committed to Equity, Diversity, and Inclusion (EDI) and applicants are encouraged to self-identity if they are part of a marginalised community, or have experience working with Indigenous communities. If we contact you for an interview and you are a person with a disability who requires technical aids or alternative arrangements, please let us know of these needs and how we can be of assistance. Cape Breton University Human Resources Dept. HumanResouces@cbu.ca 1250 Grand Lake Road, Sydney, NS B1M 1A2 Scan this QR code and apply! Download Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Statement of Accessibility Cookie Preferences Delete Application Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/cbu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/1516": {
      "title": "Sessional Practice (Clinical)- School of Nursing",
      "description": "Sessional Practice (Clinical)- School of Nursing | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs CBU home English (United States) Sign In Sessional Practice (Clinical)- School of Nursing Req #237 Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada Apply Share Job Description Posted Thursday, October 8, 2026 at 7:00 PM | Expires Thursday, December 31, 2026 at 6:59 PM EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY Please ensure you upload your resume, attach a cover letter,  list of references in the correct upload area. Any other documents required please add to Additional Documents. Sessional Practice Nursing Pool Cape Breton University invites expressions of interest from individuals qualified in serving Practice Sessional Instructors within the School of Nursing . These appointments are made on an as-needed basis to support student clinical learning experiences throughout the academic year. Position Overview Practice Sessional Instructors are responsible for supervising and supporting nursing students in clinical practice settings while facilitating the integration of theory and practice. Instructors provide guidance, assessment, and feedback to students while ensuring safe, professional, and evidence-informed nursing care. Appointments are typically for 4-6 week clinical placements and may involve working with students from any of the School of Nursing cohorts across Terms 3 to 6. Clinical Placement Locations Clinical placements may occur in a variety of healthcare settings throughout the Cape Breton Regional Municipality (CBRM), including: Cape Breton Regional Hospital Glace Bay Hospital New Waterford Consolidated Hospital Northside General Hospital Long-term care facilities and nursing homes throughout the CBRM Responsibilities The Practice Sessional Instructor will: Supervise and mentor nursing students in clinical practice settings. Facilitate student learning and professional development. Evaluate student performance in accordance with School of Nursing policies and clinical learning outcomes. Foster safe, ethical, and professional nursing practice. Communicate and collaborate with healthcare facility staff and School of Nursing faculty. Maintain required clinical and educational documentation. Qualifications Applicants must possess: Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BScN) and current registration as a Registered Nurse (RN); or Registered Nurse Diploma and current registration as a Registered Nurse (RN). Preference may be given to applicants with: Recent clinical nursing experience. Experience teaching, preceptoring, or mentoring nursing students. Demonstrated excellence in communication, leadership, and clinical practice. Applications for the successful candidate will include a: A cover letter outlining their qualifications, clinical experience, and interest. complete resume proof of RN registration/licensure. list of at least three references. Short listed candidates will be required to submit three reference letters. Please upload all required documents to Additional Documents if no designated area is listed . Incomplete applications will not be considered. Applications will be reviewed as clinical instructional needs arise. Applica nt pool is open until December 31, 2026. Cape Breton University is strongly committed to fostering diversity within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, visible minorities, Indigenous peoples, persons with disabilities, and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply but applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. CBU is committed to Equity, Diversity, and Inclusion (EDI) and applicants are encouraged to self-identity if they are part of a marginalised community, or have experience working with Indigenous communities. If we contact you for an interview and you are a person with a disability who requires technical aids or alternative arrangements, please let us know of these needs and how we can be of assistance. Cape Breton University Human Resources Dept. HumanResouces@cbu.ca 1250 Grand Lake Road, Sydney, NS B1M 1A2 Scan this QR code and apply! Download Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Statement of Accessibility Cookie Preferences Delete Application Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
