    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/cbu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/1574": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant, SASS",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant, SASS | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs CBU home English (United States) Sign In Administrative Assistant, SASS Req #246 Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada Apply Share Job Description Posted Monday, October 26, 2026 at 7:00 PM | Expires Tuesday, November 10, 2026 at 6:59 PM EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY Please ensure you upload your resume, attach a cover letter,  list of references in the correct upload area. Any other documents required please add to Additional Documents. Cape Breton University (CBU) is looking for an Administrative Assistant in the School of Arts and Social Sciences. This will be approximately 10-month limited term . Reporting to the Dean, collaborate with the administrative team of SASS to support a range of academic policies, procedures, services, and events. The administrative team of SASS includes department chairs, associate dean, executive assistant to the dean, and dean. SPECIFIC RESPONSIBILITIES: Provide comprehensive administrative support to department chairs and the Bachelor of Social Work Program , including academic timetable development, enrollment and course administration, waitlist and field placement coordination, faculty advising scheduling, admissions and practicum support, and participation in school-based committees and working groups. Participate in university events (e.g. strategic planning sessions or orientation) and attend professional development seminars, workshops, and conferences, as appropriate. Generate analytical reports using university ERP systems (Colleague, Advise, Recruit) and support Quality Assurance initiatives through research, auditing, report writing, and operational reviews to inform departmental and program decision-making. Other related duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS: A diploma or degree in a relevant area of study or practice ; Minimum of demonstrated three years of recent related experience (education/academic environment preferred); Demonstrated experience working in a fast-paced, office environment with complex changing priorities on a day-to day basis; Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, both oral and written, and ability to work with a wide range of clients with diverse needs and backgrounds; Ability to work in a team environment, and maintain good working relationships with other university employees; Good organizational skills, personal judgment, and ability to maintain confidentiality; High level of proficiency with MS Office, including Teams, Word, Excel, and PowerPoint, and ability to learn updated and/or new software, applications, and digital tools/systems quickly, including the CBU student information system. Applications for the successful candidate will include a: cover letter describing the expertise of the applicant complete resume list of at least three references. Please upload all required documents to Additional Documents if no designated area is listed . Incomplete applications may not be considered. Applications must be received by 11:00PM on November 10th, 2026. The union affiliation of this position is with the Canadian Union of Public Employees (CUPE) Local 3131. Salary level is Band A5. Cape Breton University is strongly committed to fostering diversity within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, visible minorities, Indigenous peoples, persons with disabilities, and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply but applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. CBU is committed to Equity, Diversity, and Inclusion (EDI) and applicants are encouraged to self-identity if they are part of a marginalised community, or have experience working with Indigenous communities. If we contact you for an interview and you are a person with a disability who requires technical aids or alternative arrangements, please let us know of these needs and how we can be of assistance. Cape Breton University Human Resources Dept. HumanResouces@cbu.ca 1250 Grand Lake Road, Sydney, NS B1M 1A2 Scan this QR code and apply! Download Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Statement of Accessibility Cookie Preferences Delete Application Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/cbu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/1561": {
      "title": "Clerkship Coordinator",
      "description": "Clerkship Coordinator – MED 3-4  | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs CBU home English (United States) Sign In Clerkship Coordinator – MED 3-4 Req #234 CBU, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada Apply Share Job Description Posted Thursday, October 22, 2026 at 7:00 PM | Expires Sunday, November 15, 2026 at 6:59 PM EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY Please ensure you upload your resume, attach a cover letter,  list of references in the correct upload area. Any other documents required please add to Additional Documents. Position Type: Full-Time, Continuing Location: Cape Breton Medical Campus (CBMC) About The Campus: Dalhousie University and Cape Breton University entered a partnership in 2022 to establish the Cape Breton Medical Campus in Sydney, NS, with a goal of admitting the first cohort of learners in 2025. CBMC supports Nova Scotia's health reform agenda by training culturally competent rural physicians, advancing collaborative care, and expanding interprofessional education. The campus is dedicated to increasing specialist capacity in rural communities and improving health outcomes through targeted research in aging, frailty, L'nu (Indigenous) health , and African Nova Scotian health . Shape the Future of Rural Medicine in Nova Scotia: The Clerkship Curriculum Coordinator manages the administrative, operational, and logistical execution of clinical rotations for third- and fourth-year medical students. Reporting to the UGME Operations Manager, you will serve as the primary link between students, healthcare sites, faculty preceptors, and university administration. Core Responsibilities: Rotation Scheduling: Design complex clinical rotation templates, secure learner placements with healthcare partners, and manage campus room bookings. Assessment & Integrity: Audit faculty evaluations, manage student grades in medical education databases (One45, Brightspace, DalMedIx), and proctor examinations. Faculty Support: Track and validate clinical teaching hours for payroll, and onboard new preceptors on curriculum and portal navigation. Compliance & Committee Service: Compile accreditation data (CACMS/LCME) and provide administrative support to the Med 3 & 4 Clerkship Committee. Qualifications And Skills: Education : A Bachelor’s degree in business, education, or healthcare administration is typically preferred, or an equivalent mix of office administration diplomas and experience. Experience : Requires 5 years of professional administration experience, ideally in post-secondary institutions or hospital-based medical education programs. Technical & Soft Competencies: Medical Systems Literacy : Direct familiarity with specialized educational software (e.g., One45, DalMedIx, Brightspace, or local health authority databases). Calendar Management : The ability to build, resolve, and audit multi-layered rosters with highly variable clinical schedules. Clear Communication : High emotional intelligence and clarity when interacting with stressed learners, busy clinicians, and educational regulators. Autonomous Prioritization : Sharp troubleshooting capabilities to resolve scheduling conflicts, student absences, or clinic cancellations independently. Ready to Apply? Applications for the successful candidate will include a: cover letter describing the expertise of the applicant complete resume list of at least three references. Please upload all required documents to Additional Documents if no designated area is listed . Incomplete applications will not be considered. Applications must be received by 11:00PM on November 15, 2026 . Cape Breton University is strongly committed to fostering diversity within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, visible minorities, Indigenous peoples, persons with disabilities, and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply but applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. CBU is committed to Equity, Diversity, and Inclusion (EDI) and applicants are encouraged to self-identity if they are part of a marginalised community, or have experience working with Indigenous communities. If we contact you for an interview and you are a person with a disability who requires technical aids or alternative arrangements, please let us know of these needs and how we can be of assistance. Cape Breton University Human Resources Dept. HumanResouces@cbu.ca 1250 Grand Lake Road, Sydney, NS B1M 1A2 Scan this QR code and apply! Download CBU, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Statement of Accessibility Cookie Preferences Delete Application Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/cbu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/1557": {
      "title": "Project Manager (Homeward Bound)",
      "description": "Project Manager (Homeward Bound)  | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs CBU home English (United States) Sign In Project Manager (Homeward Bound) Req #243 Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada Apply Share Job Description Posted Wednesday, October 21, 2026 at 7:00 PM | Expires Friday, November 6, 2026 at 6:59 PM EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY Please ensure you upload your resume, attach a cover letter,  list of references in the correct upload area. Any other documents required please add to Additional Documents. Cape Breton University (CBU) is accepting applications for a Project Manager to join a transformative, multi-year research initiative titled Homeward Bound: Enhancing Healthcare, Housing, and Social Support for Aging Rural Nova Scotians . Funded by Research Nova Scotia, this 7-year initiative aims to support aging in the right place (AIRP) by improving the integration of healthcare, housing, and social supports in rural communities across Nova Scotia’s Eastern Health Zone. This ambitious project brings together a multidisciplinary team spanning social work, architecture, nursing, medicine, computer science, economics, and policy, in partnership with communities, government, and academic institutions. Find out more here : www.homewardboundns.ca About the Role We are seeking a Project Manager to join our unique and innovative project. This position requires strong communication skills, exceptional attention to detail, and the ability to coordinate large teams. As a Project Manager, you will play a key leadership role in shaping and executing a transformative initiative, working closely with a dynamic team of experts. This is a full-time, hybrid position reporting to the Co-Principal Investigator overseeing Research Operations ( Dr. Kelsey Harvey ) and working within a multidisciplinary team . The appointment is for one year, with the possibility of renewal. S alary Range: 80,000 – 90,000 SPECIFIC RESPONSIBILITIES: Steward and refine a project management system, develop and report on detailed project plans, milestones, and schedules and ensure adherence across all projects; Identify and managing infrastructure, resources, and vendor-related activities as per project requirements; Collaborate with CBU Human Resources for project hiring; Draft and post job ads, schedule interviews, sit on hiring panels as needed, issue contracts, manage project onboarding, and track appointment renewals for staff, postdocs and student research assistants (including Mitacs placements); Keep a project staffing plan and onboarding checklist covering accounts, training, REB/TCPS 2 certification and confidentiality agreements; Oversee and communicate project progress and status to team members or collaborators; Identify and manage project risks and issues; Devise remedial actions for any identified issues, alert upwards (project governance council). and conduct crisis management when necessary; Facilitate communication and collaboration across all areas of the project. Develop and maintain project documentation including standard operating procedures; Initiate planning with the research team, follow-through on the plans, ensure smooth execution of the plans, and evaluate the project for further improvements should these be needed; Assist the Research Manager with project budgets, including invoice preparations, budget tracking, and other related tasks; Work closely with the Knowledge Mobilization Specialist to align project timelines, milestones and research outputs with the KM and communications plan; Co-plan project events (conferences, workshops, community sessions, co-design sessions) with the KM Specialist (The Project Manager leads logistics, budget, travel, venues, vendors and accessibility. The KM Manager leads content, promotion, registration and post-event reporting.); Manage the different sub-project teams, ensuring seamless coordination and efficient operations; Provide support to the project’s Governance Collective; Conduct project phase post-mortems to identify lessons learned and areas for improvement; Other related duties as required. Required Qualifications: Undergraduate degree in business administration, Project Management, or a related field , or equivalent combination of education and experience ; Minimum 3+ years working as project manager on projects valued at +1M annually Knowledge of research governance principles and managerial best practices; Excellent analytical skills with the ability to track and interpret data to inform decision-making; Proficiency with all aspects of Office 365 and ability to become proficient in project management and other software systems used by the team; Experience in delivering status updates/performance reports to funder, partners, governance collectives; Excellent ability to manage multiple tasks simultaneously and solve problems creatively and under pressure; Demonstrated excellent interpersonal communication and writing skills; Experience working successfully both independently and in team environments; Proven analytical and organizational skills to meet deadlines in an environment of often-changing priorities and multiple projects. Conceptual thinker comfortable with ambiguity; Strong understanding of project management methodologies within large research projects; Commitment to respecting a high level of confidentiality; Experience in diverse multidisciplinary setting, such as medical, public, private industry, or academic environments, is considered an asset; Experience with community-based participatory research and clinical research; A commitment to understanding and aiding in the pursuit of equity, diversity and inclusion within project environments as well as working ethically; Willing and able to travel throughout the Eastern Health Zone of Nova Scotia and possibly beyond; Position will require some evening/weekend event attendance , but day-to-day working hours will be made flexible to accommodate . Preferred Qualifications: Graduate-degree preferred; Project Management Professional (PMP) certification is an asset; Knowledge of how to use Power BI Applications for the successful candidate will include a: cover letter describing the expertise of the applicant complete resume list of at least three references. Please upload all required documents to Additional Documents if no designated area is listed . Incomplete applications may not be considered. Cape Breton University is strongly committed to fostering diversity within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, visible minorities, Indigenous peoples, persons with disabilities, and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply but applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. CBU is committed to Equity, Diversity, and Inclusion (EDI) and applicants are encouraged to self-identity if they are part of a marginalised community, or have experience working with Indigenous communities. If we contact you for an interview and you are a person with a disability who requires technical aids or alternative arrangements, please let us know of these needs and how we can be of assistance. Cape Breton University Human Resources Dept. HumanResouces@cbu.ca 1250 Grand Lake Road, Sydney, NS B1M 1A2 Job Details Travel Required Yes Hiring Min Rate 80,000 CAD Hiring Max Rate 90,000 CAD Scan this QR code and apply! Download Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Statement of Accessibility Cookie Preferences Delete Application Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    }
